Upstream Data Source Attribution
--------------------------------
When publishing models, analyses, or derivative works using specific layers of
this database, please also cite the corresponding primary data sources:

1. CONUS Soil Properties (`soil_properties_conus` / `conus_variables.nc`):
    Harmonized 0-30 cm soil physical and chemical point observations across the
   Contiguous United States (50,116 observations compiled from master CONUS soil
   pedon datasets; e.g., USDA-NRCS National Cooperative Soil Survey [NCSS] /
   Rapid Carbon Assessment [RaCA] harmonized compilations).

2. Fine-Root Ecology Database (`FRED`; `fred_*` records in root tables):
   Iversen, C. M., McCormack, M. L., Powell, A. S., et al. (2017). A global
   Fine-Root Ecology Database to address below-ground challenges in plant
   ecology. New Phytologist, 215(1), 15-26. https://roots.ornl.gov/

3. TRY Plant Trait Database (`TRY`; `try_*` records in root tables):
   Kattge, J., Bonisch, G., Diaz, S., et al. (2020). TRY plant trait database -
   enhanced coverage and open access. Global Change Biology, 26(1), 119-188.
   https://www.try-db.org/ (TRY open-access data released under CC-BY).

4. Soil Microbial Functional Enzyme Encoding Genes (`microbe_*` tables):
   Scaled relative abundances (0-1) of carbon (C), nitrogen (N), and phosphorus
   (P) degrading microbial enzyme encoding genes across 805 CONUS locations.

